==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|tumour}}, from {{der|en|fro|tumour}}, from {{der|en|la|tumor|t=swelling}}, from {{m|la|tumeō|t=bulge, swell|pos=verb}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*tewh₂-|t=to swell}}. Related to {{cog|en|thumb}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|oncology|pathology}} An abnormal [[growth]]; [[differential diagnosis]] includes [[abscess]], [[metaplasia]], and [[neoplasia]].

====Usage notes====
{{m|en|tumour|Tumour}} is the favoured spelling throughout the [[Anglosphere|English-speaking world]] with the exception of the [[United States]], where {{m|en|tumor}} is standard.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|tumourigenesis}}

